@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.814 = private unnamed_addr constant [28 x i8] c"complex-if-statement-in-stub", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.815 = private unnamed_addr constant [683 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `if` statements with complex conditionals in stubs.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AType checkers understand simple conditionals to express variations between\0Adifferent Python versions and platforms. However, complex tests may not be\0Aunderstood by a type checker, leading to incorrect inferences when they\0Aanalyze your code.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif (3, 10) <= sys.version_info < (3, 12): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info >= (3, 10) and sys.version_info < (3, 12): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Version and platform checking](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/directives.html#version-and-platform-checks)\0A", align 1
