@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.923 = private unnamed_addr constant [2392 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for doc lines that exceed the specified maximum character length.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFor flowing long blocks of text (docstrings or comments), overlong lines\0Acan hurt readability. [PEP 8], for example, recommends that such lines be\0Alimited to 72 characters, while this rule enforces the limit specified by\0Athe [`lint.pycodestyle.max-doc-length`] setting. (If no value is provided, this\0Arule will be ignored, even if it's added to your `--select` list.)\0A\0AIn the context of this rule, a \22doc line\22 is defined as a line consisting\0Aof either a standalone comment or a standalone string, like a docstring.\0A\0AIn the interest of pragmatism, this rule makes a few exceptions when\0Adetermining whether a line is overlong. Namely, it:\0A\0A1. Ignores lines that consist of a single \22word\22 (i.e., without any\0A   whitespace between its characters).\0A2. Ignores lines that end with a URL, as long as the URL starts before\0A   the line-length threshold.\0A3. Ignores line that end with a pragma comment (e.g., `# type: ignore`\0A   or `# noqa`), as long as the pragma comment starts before the\0A   line-length threshold. That is, a line will not be flagged as\0A   overlong if a pragma comment _causes_ it to exceed the line length.\0A   (This behavior aligns with that of the Ruff formatter.)\0A\0AIf [`lint.pycodestyle.ignore-overlong-task-comments`] is `true`, this rule will\0Aalso ignore comments that start with any of the specified [`lint.task-tags`]\0A(e.g., `# TODO:`).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef function(x):\0A    \22\22\22Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Duis auctor purus ut ex fermentum, at maximus est hendrerit.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef function(x):\0A    \22\22\22\0A    Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.\0A    Duis auctor purus ut ex fermentum, at maximus est hendrerit.\0A    \22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Error suppression\0AHint: when suppressing `W505` errors within multi-line strings (like\0Adocstrings), the `noqa` directive should come at the end of the string\0A(after the closing triple quote), and will apply to the entire string, like\0Aso:\0A\0A```python\0A\22\22\22Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet.\0A\0ALorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor.\0A\22\22\22  # noqa: W505\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.task-tags`\0A- `lint.pycodestyle.max-doc-length`\0A- `lint.pycodestyle.ignore-overlong-task-comments`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#maximum-line-length\0A", align 1
