@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.963 = private unnamed_addr constant [461 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for a # symbol appearing on a line not followed by an actual comment.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AEmpty comments don't provide any clarity to the code, and just add clutter.\0AEither add a comment or delete the empty comment.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:  #\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Pylint documentation](https://pylint.pycqa.org/en/latest/user_guide/messages/refactor/empty-comment.html)\0A", align 1
