@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.979 = private unnamed_addr constant [873 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of unnamed numerical constants (\22magic\22) values in\0Acomparisons.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe use of \22magic\22 values can make code harder to read and maintain, as\0Areaders will have to infer the meaning of the value from the context.\0ASuch values are discouraged by [PEP 8].\0A\0AFor convenience, this rule excludes a variety of common values from the\0A\22magic\22 value definition, such as `0`, `1`, `\22\22`, and `\22__main__\22`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef apply_discount(price: float) -> float:\0A    if price <= 100:\0A        return price / 2\0A    else:\0A        return price\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0AMAX_DISCOUNT = 100\0A\0A\0Adef apply_discount(price: float) -> float:\0A    if price <= MAX_DISCOUNT:\0A        return price / 2\0A    else:\0A        return price\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pylint.allow-magic-value-types`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#constants\0A", align 1
